<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75368" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρσο-θύρη</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῠ]</span>, ἡ, prob. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a door high up
				in the wall,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				22.126
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				333
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀν᾽ ὀρσοθύρην ἀναβαίη</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				132
			</span></i> : sens. obsc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς ὄπισθεν ὀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Semon.
					17
				</span></i>
			 [where <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">υ</span> appears to be long].
				(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θύρα ἐν ὕψει τοῦ τοίχου,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>, cf. the second explanation in <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>: a form <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρσορόκα</span> (acc.
			sg.) given by <i><span class="en">
				Apollod.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				633.57
			</span></i> sqq. is apptly. corrupt:— <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρσοθύρη</span> was derived in antiquity from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρούω,</span>
			<u>EM</u> l. c., etc.: the true etym. is uncertain, but cf.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρρος, ὀρρόβηλος.</span>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
